## Types

```mdl
type CodeGraph
  desc: A curated view of the code index. Boxes and arrows are held inline; each box stands for a resource in the index.
  fields:
    name?: string
    layout?: Layout
    nodes: Node[]
    edges: Edge[]

type Node
  desc: One box.
  fields:
    id: string             # the resource IRI, e.g. https://dxos.org/deus/package/@dxos/echo
    label: string
    kind: NodeKind
    group?: string         # the package directory; the illustrator frames boxes by it
    position?: Position    # where the user dragged the box

type Edge
  desc: One arrow, from the subject to the object of a triple.
  fields:
    from: string
    to: string
    kind?: string          # the predicate's local name, e.g. imports, usesPackage

type NodeKind
  literals: package | file | symbol | module | spec | other

type Layout
  literals: illustrator | force | rank | diagram
```

## Operations

```mdl
op query
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.query
  desc: Runs a SPARQL SELECT over the index and returns the rows; draws nothing.

op inspect
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.inspect
  desc: Returns one resource's outgoing facts and incoming counts.

op read
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.read
  desc: Returns a graph's boxes, arrows and layout.

op addFromQuery
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.addFromQuery
  desc: Runs a SELECT and draws its rows; ?from/?to rows are arrows, ?node rows are boxes.

op addNodes
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.addNodes
  desc: Adds boxes for resources and connects every box pair the index links by imports or usesPackage.

op addNeighbors
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.addNeighbors
  desc: Adds the neighbours of boxes along one predicate, outward, inward or both.

op remove
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.remove
  desc: Removes boxes and their arrows, or everything.

op setLayout
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.setLayout
  desc: Chooses the layout, and optionally forgets dragged positions.
```

## Components

```mdl
component CodeGraphArticle
  desc: The article surface. A toolbar picks the layout and resets positions; the body is the canvas or the drawing, with a details panel for the selected box.
  props:
    subject: CodeGraph

component CodeGraphCanvas
  desc: react-ui-canvas's dynamic projection with one box per resource, as plugin-projects' FeatureCanvas uses it. Arrangement and an overlay of positions place the boxes.

component CodeGraphDiagram
  desc: plugin-illustrator's SceneSvg drawing of the semantic layout, read-only, with package frames and routed arrows.

component NodeDetails
  desc: The selected resource's facts, with expand and remove actions.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Read the index from the app
  req F-1.1: A same-origin dev-server route answers read-only code-index tools by running `code-index mcp` as a child process.
  req F-1.2: The route accepts only loopback callers and JSON requests, so other pages and machines cannot read the source tree.
  req F-1.3: Without the route (a deployed build), every operation fails with an error that names the missing route.

feat F-2: The assistant shapes the graph
  req F-2.1: The Code Graph skill offers query, inspect, read, addFromQuery, addNodes, addNeighbors, remove and setLayout, and the space's addObject to create a graph.
  req F-2.2: A chat about a CodeGraph object carries the skill (SkillsAnnotation).
  req F-2.3: Adding never duplicates a box or an arrow, and a box an arrow needs is added with it.

feat F-3: Two layouts on one canvas
  req F-3.1: The illustrator layout solves the graph as semantic DSL and places canvas boxes at the solved centres, framing boxes by package when there are 2 to 6 packages.
  req F-3.2: The force layout uses the canvas's own force arrangement; rank uses its fewest-crossings arrangement.
  req F-3.3: Dragging a box saves only its position; boxes the user did not move stay under the layout.
  req F-3.4: The diagram layout renders the illustrator's full drawing with SceneSvg.

feat F-4: Inspect a box
  req F-4.1: Double-clicking a box opens its facts from the index.
  req F-4.2: The details panel expands the box's dependencies or dependents, or removes it.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Draw package dependencies
  given: an index of this repository, and composer-app under `vite dev`
  when: the assistant is asked to draw the @dxos packages plugin-markdown depends on
  then: a code graph shows plugin-markdown with an arrow to each dependency, laid out by the illustrator

scenario T-2: Switch layout
  given: a code graph with boxes
  when: the user picks the force layout
  then: the same boxes are re-placed by the force arrangement, and the graph's layout field reads force
```

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: Draw and reshape a package graph
  desc: The primary journey — create a graph, fill it from the index, expand a box, switch layouts.
  actors: human, agent
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.3, F-3.1, F-3.2]
  status: passing           # 2026-10-23; driven by a Playwright script against `vite dev`: steps 1-3 by `invoke`, step 4 and the details panel's Expand by clicks. The assistant chat itself was not exercised (no model key in the sandbox).
  given:
    - the index is built (`bun tools/code-index/bin/code-index.ts index`) and no other code-index process holds it
    - composer-app runs under `moon run composer-app:serve`
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-code-graph is enabled
  steps:
    - name: Create the graph
      do: In the navtree, click + and choose Code Graph. Name it "QA Code Graph".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: { "@type": "org.dxos.type.codeGraph", name: "QA Code Graph", nodes: [], edges: [] } }
      capture: graph
      expect: an empty Code Graph article opens with the message asking the assistant to draw here
    - name: Draw a package's dependencies
      do: Ask the assistant to draw the @dxos packages that @dxos/plugin-markdown depends on.
      invoke: [op:addFromQuery] { graph: $graph.object, sparql: "SELECT ?from ?to WHERE { BIND(<https://dxos.org/deus/package/@dxos/plugin-markdown> AS ?from) ?from deus:usesPackage ?to . ?to deus:name ?name . FILTER(STRSTARTS(?name, \"@dxos/\")) }" }
      expect: boxes for plugin-markdown and its @dxos dependencies, with arrows from plugin-markdown, placed on a grid
      assert: return $result.addedEdges > 0 && $result.nodes === $result.addedNodes;
    - name: Expand a dependency
      do: Double-click the @dxos/echo box and choose Expand dependencies.
      invoke: [op:addNeighbors] { graph: $graph.object, nodes: ["pkg:@dxos/echo"] }
      expect: the packages echo depends on appear, with arrows from echo
      assert: return $result.addedNodes > 0;
    - name: Switch to the force layout
      do: Click the force-directed layout button in the toolbar.
      invoke: [op:setLayout] { graph: $graph.object, layout: "force" }
      expect: the same boxes are re-placed; none overlap
  after:
    - name: Delete the graph
      do: Right-click "QA Code Graph" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      expect: the graph leaves the navtree
```

## Changelog

Every change to this spec adds a decision, newest last. See `lang/changelog.mdl` for the attribution rules.

```mdl
decision D-1: A Composer plugin integrates with code-index; it may work only under `vite dev` or in Tauri.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The plugin's article is a canvas of the code graph, and the assistant gets tools to query and change that graph.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodeGraphArticle, F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The canvas lays the graph out both with the illustrator's layout and as a force-directed graph, sharing the canvas and illustrator code the way feature maps do.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodeGraphCanvas, F-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: The page reaches code-index through a dev-server route that runs `code-index mcp` as a child process. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.2]
  why: The index's store is single-process behind a native addon, and the code-index web server has no SPARQL route; the MCP server already serves the read-only tools.
  rejected: Opening the store in the vite process, which would hold its lock and load the addon there.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: One canvas serves the illustrator, force and rank layouts; the illustrator's semantic engine supplies box positions as the canvas overlay, and a fourth view shows the illustrator's own drawing. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodeGraphCanvas, CodeGraphDiagram, F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.4]
  why: Feature maps use react-ui-canvas's dynamic projection, which already has a force arrangement; feeding it illustrator positions compares both layouts on one component.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: Illustrator positions are centred on the origin, and the canvas refits when they arrive. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodeGraphCanvas, F-3.1]
  why: The engine's coordinates start at its own origin and arrive after the canvas's first fit, so the graph opened off-centre and too small to read.
```
